WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.330
Hi, I'm Brian with Top Notch Lawn Care.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:16.980
We specialize in taking
overgrown, out-of-shape properties

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:20.263
and getting these properties
back into a manageable state.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.400
Today, I'm going to take
you guys through the process

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.650
of getting this overgrown
property back into shape.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.610
On this property here,

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:32.920
the first thing we're going to do

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.510
is we're going to blow off the patio

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:36.310
to expose what's underneath there

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:37.960
and to see what needs to be done.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.230
Walking into this backyard,

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:41.210
it was very evident

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:43.760
this property hasn't been
maintained in a long time.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.443
I'm guessing probably at
least a year to two years.

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:49.960
You can tell that by all
the weeds in the cracks,

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:51.400
all the overgrown edging,

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.980
and the very tall grass in the lawn.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:56.020
Then we are going to trim and edge

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.700
and then we're going to
finish off with mowing.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:00.560
That way we can get all the
trimming and edging clippings

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.560
back into the lawn

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.633
and mulch those up with the grass.

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:06.900
Not only did we transform the backyard,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.650
we transformed the front yard
on this property as well.

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:12.900
In this job in particular,

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:16.110
we had to move all the furniture
to one side of the patio

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:19.050
so we can get all the weeds
out of the patio cracks

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:20.500
and make it look really good.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.170
Blowing off first is not
something I normally do

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:25.390
on these types of projects.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:28.290
But on this project here,
I felt it was necessary.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.230
So that way I could see all the weeds

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:32.930
coming through the cracks
to make sure I got them all.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.160
So after that, we're going
to start with the trimming.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:37.780
And I started with the patio first

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:40.180
to get all the weeds out of the cracks.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:42.020
I started with the side of the garage,

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:44.140
worked my way around to
the back of the garage

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:45.973
and then just around the fence.

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:49.960
In order to not damage
any of the perimeter,

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.870
whether it being the house or the fence,

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:54.820
we used the trimmer to get the
areas that the mower cannot.

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:59.210
The rotation of the trimmer
head goes from right to left.

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:01.350
So if you trim from right to left,

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:04.100
it blows the clippings
left back into the lawn.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.790
I started on the right
side of this property

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:06.623
with the trimming.

00:02:06.623 --> 00:02:10.070
That way, I can control
where the clipping shoot out.

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:11.660
If you start from right to left,

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:14.890
the clippings will shoot
out left, back into the lawn

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:17.290
and that way you don't
have to worry about them.

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:22.010
Once the trimming is done,

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:23.490
I will move on to the edging

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.870
to clean up the patio and the sidewalk.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:27.040
The purpose for edging

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.750
is to give it a nice, clean, crisp look

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:33.463
to separate the lawn from
the patio and the sidewalk.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:40.790
I will start edging on the
right side of the patio

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:43.730
and I will work my way down the sidewalk,

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.020
back up the sidewalk

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:47.670
and then finish off with
the other side of the patio.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:53.487
I usually just start on one
side, I'll finish on the other.

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:01.680
The biggest reason why we
start with this process

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.470
of trimming and edging first

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:05.300
is so we can get all the clippings

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:08.500
from the trimming and edging
process back into the lawn

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.470
so when we mow, we're
not mowing multiple times

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:14.070
and we can actually mulch
it up with the tall grass.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:17.720
After the trimming and edging is complete,

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:18.990
I'll take the leaf blower,

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:21.220
blow all the debris back into the lawn

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:22.503
so I can mow it up.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:25.480
The final step in this process

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:27.053
is going to be mowing the lawn.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:34.540
I always start at a higher
height when I'm cutting the lawn

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.340
and then I'll go over it a second time

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:37.543
decreasing that height.

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:40.160
Most of the time,

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.280
my desired height that I'm aiming for

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:43.863
is right at three inches.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.710
Be very careful when you're mowing

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:48.150
an overgrown lawn like this,

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:50.520
because you can't see what's in the grass.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.980
There's a lot of things
like debris, rocks, bricks,

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.970
and sometimes even concrete.

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:58.530
And you can actually throw
stuff out of your mower

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:01.613
that could damage a house or a fence.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:20.963
So lastly,

00:04:20.963 --> 00:04:22.870
I'm going to blow off one more time

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:25.780
just to get all the
remaining grass and dust

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.830
and reposition the
furniture back on the patio.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:29.960
From start to finish,

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:32.550
this job took us right
around four and a half hours

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:34.200
to complete.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.160
If you want a nice healthy lawn,

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.670
I recommend mowing once a
week or once every two weeks,

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.120
depending on your grass type.

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:45.420
It was very satisfying to hear
how shocked the homeowner was

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:47.337
at this transformation.

